# Glyph map for The New Oxford American Dictionary (american.mobi).
#
# NOAD-for-Kindle renders its pronunciation respelling, section headings and
# sense markers as one tiny GIF per character.  This table replaces them with
# real text, which makes the result searchable, selectable and legible at any
# font size.  Derived by decoding known pronunciations (lamb, father, though,
# ship, measure, loch, sing, boot, book, water, machine, ...) until every
# transcription matched NOAD.
#
# Format: <recindex>[,<recindex>...] TAB <replacement> [TAB <comment>]
# A comma-separated list matches that run of consecutive images.
# No replacement field means "drop it"; \s in a replacement means a space.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
# Unmapped images are still extracted to res/ and referenced normally.

# --- pronunciation delimiters and stress ---------------------------------
10	|	between-pronunciation bars
46	|	italic bar, used in usage notes
1060	|
54	ˈ	primary stress
874	ˈ	italic primary stress
58	ˌ	secondary stress
37	;\s	separates variant pronunciations (\s = a literal space)
111	-

